{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch8N71CN7UuKNRng2uS9M","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The greeting moves from `main.go` into `internal/render` as `Greeting(name)`, which returns green \"hello\" followed by the name, defaulting to \"world\". The command moves to `cmd/demo`, reads its name from the first argument, and prints the result. The colour codes are applied unconditionally, so output contains escape codes whether or not it goes to a terminal.\n\n## differs\n- The greeting now takes a name: it prints `hello, <name>`, or `hello, world` with no argument, where the old code always printed a fixed `hello`.\n- The colour codes are applied unconditionally, so piped output contains escape codes.\n- The change adds a test, `internal/render/render_test.go`, which the description doesn't mention.\n\n## read: the greeting and the code that prints it\nStart with what `Greeting` is built on, then the command that calls it, then the test.\n- internal/render/colour/colour.go: adds `Green`, which wraps text in ANSI green codes.\n- internal/render/render.go: `Greeting(name)` returns green \"hello\", then \", \" and the name, defaulting to \"world\".\n- cmd/demo/main.go: the command, which takes the name from the first argument and prints `Greeting`'s result.\n- internal/render/render_test.go: one test that `Greeting(\"ada\")` ends in \", ada\".\n\n## skim: moves, a rename and a lockfile\nThese are removed, moved or generated, so their contents are either covered above or not hand-written.\n- main.go: deleted; its greeting moved to `internal/render` and its `main` to `cmd/demo`.\n- docs/README.md: renamed from `README.md`.\n- go.sum: lockfile."}]},"session_id":"ee41dafd-48cf-49c4-82e7-fdb437303c0d","parent_tool_use_id":null}
